/-!
# Every `R`-algebra is the canonical filtered colimit of its finitely presented subalgebras

Proof of Stacks 0BUF: let `R → A` be a ring map and let `𝓘` be the category of `R`-algebra maps
`A' → A` with `A'` of finite presentation over `R`, a morphism being an `R`-algebra map over `A`.
Then `𝓘` is filtered and `A` is the colimit of the `A'` over `𝓘`, via the tautological cocone whose
leg at `A' → A` is that very map.

One construction carries both halves of the proof: if finitely many relations between elements of
an object `A' → A` of `𝓘` hold in `A`, then they hold already in an object of `𝓘` under `A'`,
namely in `A'/I` for `I` the ideal generated by the differences. The quotient is again of finite
presentation over `R` because `I` is finitely generated, and `A' → A` kills `I`, hence factors
through it. Filteredness applies this to a pair of parallel arrows `σ, τ : A' → A''` and the
relations `σ xᵢ = τ xᵢ` at a finite set of algebra generators `xᵢ` of `A'`; being a colimit
applies it to the single relation `x = y` witnessing that an element of the colimit dies in `A`.

The rest is elementary. `𝓘` contains `R = R`, and a pair of objects `A' → A`, `A'' → A` is
dominated by `A' ⊗[R] A'' → A`, which is again of finite presentation over `R` since finite
presentation is stable under base change and composition. That `A` is the colimit is checked on
underlying sets, a filtered colimit of commutative rings being the colimit of the underlying sets;
every `a ∈ A` is hit, by `R[X] → A`, `X ↦ a`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FPSubalgebras.solution`: the statement of Stacks 0BUF.

## Implementation notes

The index category `𝓘 = CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A` is not small: its objects live one
universe above its morphisms. So Mathlib's construction of filtered colimits of commutative rings,
which assumes a small index category, does not apply, and neither does the reflection instance
`ModuleCat.FilteredColimits.forget_reflectsFilteredColimits` in its analogous form, that one being
deduced from `reflectsColimit_of_reflectsIsomorphisms` and so needing the colimit to exist. One
could instead transport the problem to a small skeleton, which exists by
`CommRingCat.essentiallySmall_of_finiteType`, but only the reflection half of the theory is
needed and that half holds with no smallness hypothesis whatever. This is
`isColimitOfIsColimitForget`: a cocone in `CommRingCat` over a filtered `J : Type v` with
`Category.{w} J` arbitrary, whose underlying cocone of sets is colimiting, is itself colimiting.
Its proof is the direct one — the descending map is the map of sets, and it is a ring map because
any two elements of the tip come from a common object of the filtered `J`. In Mathlib's vocabulary
the statement is `ReflectsFilteredColimitsOfSize.{v, w} (forget CommRingCat.{u})`, which Mathlib
does not have for `CommRingCat` in any size.

The objects and morphisms of `𝓘` are handled through `R`-algebra data rather than through
`Under R` data: `objOf` packages a finitely presented `R`-algebra `B` together with `f : B →ₐ[R] A`
as an object, `homMkOf` packages an `R`-algebra map `u` over `A` as a morphism out of a given
object, and `homAlgHom` reads off the `R`-algebra map underlying a morphism. This keeps the three
constructions of the proof (the tensor product, the quotient, the polynomial ring) at the level at
which the source states them, with the `Under R` bookkeeping done once.

## References

* [StacksProject 0BUF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BUF)
-/

namespace Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FPSubalgebras

open CategoryTheory Limits TensorProduct



/-! ### Filtered cocones of commutative rings are detected on underlying sets -/

section Reflect

variable {J : Type v} [Category.{w} J] {F : J ⥤ CommRingCat.{u}} {c : Cocone F}

/-- Joint surjectivity of the legs of `c`, read off from the underlying cocone of sets. -/
private lemma exists_surj (ht : IsColimit ((forget CommRingCat.{u}).mapCocone c)) (x : c.pt) :
    ∃ (j : J) (a : F.obj j), c.ι.app j a = x :=
  Types.jointly_surjective_of_isColimit ht x

/-- Two elements of the tip of a filtered cocone come from a common object. -/
private lemma exists_pair [IsFiltered J]
    (ht : IsColimit ((forget CommRingCat.{u}).mapCocone c)) (x y : c.pt) :
    ∃ (j : J) (a b : F.obj j), c.ι.app j a = x ∧ c.ι.app j b = y := by
  obtain ⟨j₁, a, ha⟩ := exists_surj ht x
  obtain ⟨j₂, b, hb⟩ := exists_surj ht y
  exact ⟨IsFiltered.max j₁ j₂, F.map (IsFiltered.leftToMax j₁ j₂) a,
    F.map (IsFiltered.rightToMax j₁ j₂) b,
    by rw [← ha, ← c.w (IsFiltered.leftToMax j₁ j₂), CommRingCat.comp_apply],
    by rw [← hb, ← c.w (IsFiltered.rightToMax j₁ j₂), CommRingCat.comp_apply]⟩

private lemma desc_fac (ht : IsColimit ((forget CommRingCat.{u}).mapCocone c))
    (s : Cocone F) (j : J) (a : F.obj j) :
    ht.desc ((forget CommRingCat.{u}).mapCocone s) (c.ι.app j a) = s.ι.app j a :=
  congr($(ht.fac ((forget CommRingCat.{u}).mapCocone s) j) a)

/-- The map of sets descending a filtered cocone of commutative rings is a ring map: any two
elements of the tip come from a common object of the index category. -/
private def descRingHom [IsFiltered J]
    (ht : IsColimit ((forget CommRingCat.{u}).mapCocone c)) (s : Cocone F) :
    (c.pt : Type u) →+* (s.pt : Type u) where
  toFun := ht.desc ((forget CommRingCat.{u}).mapCocone s)
  map_one' := by
    rw [show (1 : c.pt) = c.ι.app IsFiltered.nonempty.some 1 from (map_one _).symm,
      desc_fac ht s, map_one]
  map_mul' x y := by
    obtain ⟨j, a, b, rfl, rfl⟩ := exists_pair ht x y
    simp only [← map_mul, desc_fac ht s]
  map_zero' := by
    rw [show (0 : c.pt) = c.ι.app IsFiltered.nonempty.some 0 from (map_zero _).symm,
      desc_fac ht s, map_zero]
  map_add' x y := by
    obtain ⟨j, a, b, rfl, rfl⟩ := exists_pair ht x y
    simp only [← map_add, desc_fac ht s]

/-- A filtered cocone in `CommRingCat` whose underlying cocone of sets is colimiting is itself
colimiting.  There is no smallness hypothesis on the index category `J`. -/
private def isColimitOfIsColimitForget [IsFiltered J]
    (ht : IsColimit ((forget CommRingCat.{u}).mapCocone c)) : IsColimit c where
  desc s := CommRingCat.ofHom (descRingHom ht s)
  fac s j := by ext a; exact desc_fac ht s j a
  uniq s m hm := by
    ext x
    obtain ⟨j, a, rfl⟩ := exists_surj ht x
    rw [show (CommRingCat.ofHom (descRingHom ht s)) (c.ι.app j a) = s.ι.app j a from
      desc_fac ht s j a, ← hm j, CommRingCat.comp_apply]

end Reflect

/-! ### The index category -/

/-- Being of finite presentation over `R`, as a property of objects of `Under R`. -/
private abbrev fpUnder (R : CommRingCat.{u}) : ObjectProperty (Under R) :=
  fun B ↦ B.hom.hom.FinitePresentation

section Index

variable {R : CommRingCat.{u}} {A : Under R}

/-- The object `B → A` of the index category attached to a finitely presented `R`-algebra `B`
together with an `R`-algebra map to `A`. -/
private def objOf (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra R B]
    (hB : Algebra.FinitePresentation R B) (f : B →ₐ[R] A) :
    CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A :=
  let Y₀ : (fpUnder R).FullSubcategory :=
    ⟨CommRingCat.mkUnder R B,
      (RingHom.finitePresentation_algebraMap (A := (R : Type u)) (B := B)).mpr hB⟩
  CostructuredArrow.mk (Y := Y₀) (show (fpUnder R).ι.obj Y₀ ⟶ A from f.toUnder)

/-- A morphism of the index category out of `X`, given by an `R`-algebra map over `A`. -/
private def homMkOf {X : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A} {C : Type u} [CommRing C]
    [Algebra R C] (hC : Algebra.FinitePresentation R C) (g : C →ₐ[R] A)
    (u : (X.left.obj : Type u) →ₐ[R] C)
    (hu : ∀ x : (X.left.obj : Type u), g (u x) = CommRingCat.toAlgHom X.hom x) :
    X ⟶ objOf C hC g :=
  CostructuredArrow.homMk
    (ObjectProperty.homMk (show X.left.obj ⟶ CommRingCat.mkUnder R C from u.toUnder))
    (by ext x; exact hu x)

/-- The `R`-algebra map underlying a morphism of the index category. -/
private def homAlgHom {X Y : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A} (σ : X ⟶ Y) :
    (X.left.obj : Type u) →ₐ[R] (Y.left.obj : Type u) :=
  CommRingCat.toAlgHom ((fpUnder R).ι.map σ.left)

/-- An object of the index category is a finitely presented `R`-algebra. -/
private lemma algebra_finitePresentation (X : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A) :
    Algebra.FinitePresentation (R : Type u) (X.left.obj : Type u) := X.left.property

/-- A morphism of the index category is a map over `A`. -/
private lemma hom_homAlgHom {X Y : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A} (σ : X ⟶ Y)
    (x : (X.left.obj : Type u)) :
    CommRingCat.toAlgHom Y.hom (homAlgHom σ x) = CommRingCat.toAlgHom X.hom x :=
  congr($(CostructuredArrow.w σ).right x)

private lemma homAlgHom_comp {X Y Z : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A} (σ : X ⟶ Y) (f : Y ⟶ Z) :
    homAlgHom (σ ≫ f) = (homAlgHom f).comp (homAlgHom σ) := rfl

/-- Morphisms of the index category are determined by the algebra maps underlying them. -/
private lemma hom_ext {X Y : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A} {σ τ : X ⟶ Y}
    (h : homAlgHom σ = homAlgHom τ) : σ = τ := by
  ext x; exact congr($h x)

/-- **The heart of the proof.** Finitely many relations `x i = y i` between elements of an object
`B → A` of the index category that hold in `A` hold already in an object of the index category
under `B`: divide `B` by the ideal `I` generated by the differences.  `B ⧸ I` is again of finite
presentation over `R` because `I` is finitely generated, and `B → A` kills `I`, hence factors
through `B ⧸ I`.

Both halves of the theorem rest on this: filteredness on the relations `σ xᵢ = τ xᵢ` at a finite
set of algebra generators `xᵢ` for a pair of parallel arrows `σ, τ`, and being a colimit on the
single relation `x = y` witnessing that an element of the colimit dies in `A`. -/
private lemma exists_hom_forall_map_eq {Y : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A} {ι : Type*}
    [Finite ι] (x y : ι → (Y.left.obj : Type u))
    (h : ∀ i, CommRingCat.toAlgHom Y.hom (x i) = CommRingCat.toAlgHom Y.hom (y i)) :
    ∃ (Z : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A) (f : Y ⟶ Z),
      ∀ i, homAlgHom f (x i) = homAlgHom f (y i) := by
  have := algebra_finitePresentation Y
  let I : Ideal (Y.left.obj : Type u) := Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ x i - y i)
  have hker : ∀ a ∈ I, (CommRingCat.toAlgHom Y.hom : (Y.left.obj : Type u) →ₐ[R] A) a = 0 :=
    fun a ha ↦ RingHom.mem_ker.1 <| Ideal.span_le.2 (Set.range_subset_iff.2 fun i ↦ by
      simpa [RingHom.mem_ker, sub_eq_zero] using h i) ha
  have hC : Algebra.FinitePresentation (R : Type u) ((Y.left.obj : Type u) ⧸ I) :=
    Algebra.FinitePresentation.quotient (Submodule.fg_span (Set.finite_range _))
  refine ⟨objOf _ hC (Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ I _ hker),
    homMkOf hC _ (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R I) fun z ↦ rfl, fun i ↦ ?_⟩
  exact (Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk_iff_sub_mem ..).2 (Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)

private lemma isFiltered_costructuredArrow (A : Under R) :
    IsFiltered (CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A) where
  nonempty := ⟨objOf (R : Type u) inferInstance (Algebra.ofId R A)⟩
  cocone_objs X Y := by
    have := algebra_finitePresentation X
    have := algebra_finitePresentation Y
    have hT : Algebra.FinitePresentation (R : Type u)
        ((X.left.obj : Type u) ⊗[(R : Type u)] (Y.left.obj : Type u)) :=
      Algebra.FinitePresentation.trans (R : Type u) (X.left.obj : Type u) _
    exact ⟨objOf _ hT (Algebra.TensorProduct.lift
        (CommRingCat.toAlgHom X.hom : (X.left.obj : Type u) →ₐ[R] A)
        (CommRingCat.toAlgHom Y.hom : (Y.left.obj : Type u) →ₐ[R] A)
        fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _),
      homMkOf hT _ Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft (fun x ↦ by simp),
      homMkOf hT _ Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (fun x ↦ by simp), trivial⟩
  cocone_maps X Y σ τ := by
    have := algebra_finitePresentation X
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.out (R := (R : Type u)) (A := (X.left.obj : Type u))
    obtain ⟨Z, f, hf⟩ := exists_hom_forall_map_eq (Y := Y)
      (x := fun i : g ↦ homAlgHom σ i.1) (y := fun i : g ↦ homAlgHom τ i.1)
      fun i ↦ (hom_homAlgHom σ i.1).trans (hom_homAlgHom τ i.1).symm
    exact ⟨Z, f, hom_ext <| by
      rw [homAlgHom_comp, homAlgHom_comp]
      exact AlgHom.ext_of_adjoin_eq_top hg fun z hz ↦ hf ⟨z, hz⟩⟩

/-- Every element of `A` is the image of an element of a finitely presented `R`-algebra over `A`:
use `R[X] → A`, `X ↦ a`. -/
private lemma exists_lift (a : (A : Type u)) :
    ∃ (X : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A) (t : (X.left.obj : Type u)),
      a = CommRingCat.toAlgHom X.hom t :=
  ⟨objOf (Polynomial (R : Type u)) inferInstance (Polynomial.aeval a), Polynomial.X,
    (Polynomial.aeval_X a).symm⟩

/-- Two elements of an object of the index category with the same image in `A` are identified
already by a morphism of the index category out of it. -/
private lemma exists_coeq (X : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A) (x y : (X.left.obj : Type u))
    (hxy : CommRingCat.toAlgHom X.hom x = CommRingCat.toAlgHom X.hom y) :
    ∃ (Z : CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A) (f : X ⟶ Z), homAlgHom f x = homAlgHom f y := by
  obtain ⟨Z, f, hf⟩ := exists_hom_forall_map_eq (x := fun _ : Unit ↦ x) (y := fun _ ↦ y)
    fun _ ↦ hxy
  exact ⟨Z, f, hf ()⟩

/-! ### `A` is the colimit of the finitely presented `R`-algebras over it -/

private lemma isDenseAt_finitePresentation (A : Under R) : (fpUnder R).ι.isDenseAt A := by
  have := isFiltered_costructuredArrow A
  have := IsFiltered.isConnected (CostructuredArrow (fpUnder R).ι A)
  exact ⟨isColimitOfReflects (Under.forget R) (isColimitOfIsColimitForget
    (Types.FilteredColimit.isColimitOf' _ _ (fun a ↦ exists_lift a)
      fun X x y hxy ↦ exists_coeq X x y hxy))⟩

end Index

/-- **Lemma 0BUF.** For an `R`-algebra `A`, the category of `R`-algebra maps `A' → A` with
`A'` of finite presentation over `R` is filtered, and `A` is the colimit of the `A'` over it. -/
public theorem solution {R : CommRingCat.{u}} (A : Under R) :
    IsFiltered (CostructuredArrow
        (ObjectProperty.ι fun B : Under R ↦ B.hom.hom.FinitePresentation) A) ∧
      (ObjectProperty.ι fun B : Under R ↦ B.hom.hom.FinitePresentation).isDenseAt A :=
  ⟨isFiltered_costructuredArrow A, isDenseAt_finitePresentation A⟩

end Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FPSubalgebras

/-!
# Every algebra is the canonical filtered colimit of its finitely presented subalgebras

Let `R → A` be a ring map and let `𝓘` be the category whose objects are the `R`-algebra
maps `A' → A` with `A'` of finite presentation over `R`, a morphism `(A' → A) ⟶ (A'' → A)`
being an `R`-algebra map `A' → A''` compatible with the maps to `A`. Then `𝓘` is filtered
and `A` is the colimit of the `A'` over `𝓘`, the colimit cocone being the tautological one
whose leg at `A' → A` is that very map.

Filteredness is elementary: `𝓘` contains `R = R`; a pair of objects `A' → A`, `A'' → A` is
dominated by `A' ⊗[R] A'' → A`, which is again of finite presentation; and a pair of
parallel arrows `σ, τ : A' → A''` is equalized by the surjection onto the finitely
presented algebra `A''/(σ(xᵢ) - τ(xᵢ))` obtained by killing the differences of the images
of a finite set of algebra generators `xᵢ` of `A'`, through which `A'' → A` factors. That
`A` is the colimit is then checked on underlying sets, a filtered colimit of rings being
the colimit of the underlying sets: every `a ∈ A` is hit, by `R[x] → A`, `x ↦ a`, and an
element of the colimit dying in `A` is represented by some `a' ∈ A'`, which dies already in
the object `A'/(a') → A` of `𝓘`.

## Main results

* `CommRingCat.isFiltered_costructuredArrow_and_isDenseAt_finitePresentation`: the category
  of finitely presented `R`-algebras over `A` is filtered, and `A` is the canonical colimit
  over it.

## Implementation notes

The category `𝓘` is spelled `CostructuredArrow P.ι A` for `A : Under R` an object of the
category of `R`-algebras and `P : ObjectProperty (Under R)` the property of being of finite
presentation over `R`: objects of `CostructuredArrow P.ι A` are pairs of a finitely
presented `R`-algebra `A'` and an `R`-algebra map `A' → A`, and morphisms are `R`-algebra
maps over `A`, which is the source's `𝓘` verbatim. `P` is inlined rather than named
because it is `Under.hom` followed by `RingHom.FinitePresentation`, with nothing to say
about it beyond this lemma.

"The colimit of the `A'` over `𝓘` is isomorphic to `A`" is spelled `P.ι.isDenseAt A`,
Mathlib's predicate saying that `A` is a *canonical colimit* relative to `P.ι`: it asserts
precisely that the tautological cocone on `CostructuredArrow.proj P.ι A ⋙ P.ι`, whose tip
is `A` and whose leg at `A' → A` is that map, is a colimit cocone (`Functor.denseAtEquiv`
unfolds it to that `IsColimit`; the tip and the legs are `rfl` and `simp` respectively).
This is stronger than a bare isomorphism `colim A' ≅ A`, which would not pin the map, and
it is stated in `Under R`, so the colimit is the colimit of `R`-algebras, as in the source.
Since `A` is arbitrary here, the statement is equivalent to `Functor.IsDense P.ι`, the
assertion that the finitely presented `R`-algebras form a dense subcategory of all
`R`-algebras.

The source's footnote restricts `𝓘` to quotients of `R[x₁, x₂, …]` to keep the index
category small. No such device is needed: `IsColimit` is a property of a cocone rather than
an existence statement, so it is meaningful for the large (but essentially small) category
`𝓘`, and it is implied by the corresponding statement for a small skeleton, whose inclusion
is final. Mathlib's `CommRingCat.essentiallySmall_of_finiteType` provides that smallness
when a proof wants it.

Mathlib knows one half of the interaction of finite presentation with the categorical
notion of presentability, namely `CommRingCat.isFinitelyPresentable_under` (a finitely
presented algebra is a finitely presentable object of `Under R`), and it knows the
factorization results `RingHom.EssFiniteType.exists_eq_comp_ι_app_of_isColimit` and
`.exists_comp_map_eq_of_isColimit` (tag 00QO), but it has neither
`IsFinitelyAccessibleCategory (Under R)` nor the present lemma.

Faithfulness. (1) There are no hypotheses beyond the data `R`, `A` and the ring map
`R → A` carried by `A : Under R`, all three of which the conclusion mentions. (2) The
scalars and the base are the source's: `Under R` makes every algebra and every map in
sight an `R`-algebra and an `R`-algebra map, and the colimit is taken in `R`-algebras, not
in rings or in sets. (3) The canonical map is pinned, not merely asserted to exist:
`isDenseAt` names the cocone whose leg at an object `A' → A` of `𝓘` *is* that structure
map, so the comparison map `colim A' → A` is the one induced by the structure maps. (4) The
instantiation is not degenerate: `𝓘` is nonempty for every `A` (it contains `R = R`, and
`R[x] → A`, `x ↦ a`, for each `a ∈ A`), and for `A = R[x₁, x₂, x₃, …]` a polynomial ring on
infinitely many variables — not itself of finite presentation — the lemma exhibits a
genuinely infinite filtered system, `A` being the colimit of its finitely generated
polynomial subalgebras.

## References

* [StacksProject 0BUF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BUF)

## Tags

filtered colimit, finite presentation, dense subcategory, canonical colimit
-/

open CategoryTheory Limits



namespace CommRingCat

/-- Let `R → A` be a ring map and let `𝓘 = CostructuredArrow P.ι A` be the category of
`R`-algebra maps `A' → A` with `A'` of finite presentation over `R`. Then `𝓘` is filtered,
and `A` is the colimit of the `A'` over `𝓘`, via the tautological cocone whose leg at
`A' → A` is that map (which is what `Functor.isDenseAt` asserts). -/
@[stacks 0BUF "The category `𝓘` is `CostructuredArrow P.ι A` for `P` the property of being
of finite presentation over `R`, and \"the colimit of the `A'` is `A`\" is
`P.ι.isDenseAt A`, which pins the colimit cocone to the tautological one. No smallness
device is needed. See the module docstring.", ega "IV 1.9.3.1" "more general"]
public theorem isFiltered_costructuredArrow_and_isDenseAt_finitePresentation
    {R : CommRingCat.{u}} (A : Under R) :
    IsFiltered (CostructuredArrow
        (ObjectProperty.ι fun B : Under R ↦ B.hom.hom.FinitePresentation) A) ∧
      (ObjectProperty.ι fun B : Under R ↦ B.hom.hom.FinitePresentation).isDenseAt A :=
    by apply Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FPSubalgebras.solution

end CommRingCat
